---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import { profilesForDomain } from '../../data/profiles';

const researchProfiles = profilesForDomain('research');
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Agentic Research Governance"
  description="A governance substrate for open-ended and agentic research: hypotheses with identity and lifecycle, evidence with provenance, and deterministic, auditable verdicts."
  pageType="Domain"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Poesis for Research · Domain</p>
      <h1>Research, constituted as a governed institution.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Agentic research fails in a recognizable pattern: hypotheses silently abandoned, budgets unspent, self-reviews ignored, rules disregarded. These are not capability gaps waiting for better models — they are institutional obligations that had no layer to live in. Poesis is that layer: the governance substrate agent frameworks lack.</p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/insights/poesis-stack-as-research-system"><Icon name="book-open" /> Read the research thesis</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/solutions/sie"><Icon name="layers" /> Explore SIE</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/contact"><Icon name="message" /> Talk to us</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--ink">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">The mental model</p>
      <h2>An institution, not a workflow.</h2>
      <p class="lead">A workflow consumes inputs and produces outputs; when it ends, nothing of it needs to remain. Research has the other character: a hypothesis has identity, an owner, and a lifecycle — abandoning it is an event, not a silence. Evidence is a claim whose weight depends on where it came from. A budget is an obligation someone answers for. None of this can live inside a reasoning trajectory or a context window; it must be the state of a governed system.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--soft">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">What the substrate provides</p>
        <h2>Five failures, one remedy: obligations with a layer to live in.</h2>
        <p class="lead">Stated as properties of the substrate — independent of any particular agent framework or model.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
        <article class="card card--feature card--static">
          <span class="tag">Ontology</span>
          <h3>What a hypothesis <em>is</em>, defined.</h3>
          <p>What a hypothesis, a budget, a review, or a deadline is must be defined before any process can be held to it. Semantics carried only in prose bind no one — GSM supplies the explicit ontology and governance grammar.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card card--feature card--static">
          <span class="tag">Identity &amp; lifecycle</span>
          <h3>Retired, not lost.</h3>
          <p>Research objects persist across trajectories, with state changes that are attributable, ordered events. What was retired remains a re-openable identity — because the record of its retirement exists.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card card--feature card--static">
          <span class="tag">Qualified evidence</span>
          <h3>Claims enter with provenance, or not at all.</h3>
          <p>An observation enters the institution with its confidence and provenance attached. Qualification does not make a claim true — it makes it governable.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card card--feature card--static">
          <span class="tag">Evaluable norms</span>
          <h3>Deviation distinguished from violation.</h3>
          <p>An hour of idleness violates nothing; chronic neglect of a mandate does. Norms carry temporal tolerance and render the difference as a verdict, not an impression.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card card--feature card--static">
          <span class="tag">Separation of powers</span>
          <h3>Measure, judge, and enforce — separately.</h3>
          <p>A process that measures, judges, and enforces itself is precisely the ungoverned condition being remedied. The layers are distinct primitives, by design.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card card--feature card--static">
          <span class="tag">Deterministic record</span>
          <h3>Verdicts anyone can recompute.</h3>
          <p>Whether an obligation was met has exactly one answer, computable from the definitions and the record. The history of decisions, evidence, and verdicts is the substrate's own queryable state — not archaeology over logs.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it compares</p>
        <h2>Trackers record. Orchestrators execute. The substrate governs.</h2>
        <p class="lead">Each tool class answers a different question — none of them carries the institution's obligations.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="compare-wrap">
        <table class="compare">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Concern</th>
              <th scope="col">Experiment tracker</th>
              <th scope="col">Agent orchestrator</th>
              <th scope="col" class="compare-poesis">Poesis substrate</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">What it holds</th>
              <td>Metrics and artifacts</td>
              <td>Workflow state</td>
              <td class="compare-poesis">Obligations, evidence, verdicts</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Hypothesis identity</th>
              <td>Tags on runs</td>
              <td>Prompt context</td>
              <td class="compare-poesis">Governed definitions with lifecycle and owners</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Rules &amp; budgets</th>
              <td>Conventions</td>
              <td>Prompt instructions</td>
              <td class="compare-poesis">Evaluable norms with temporal tolerance</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Accountability</th>
              <td>Dashboards</td>
              <td>Logs</td>
              <td class="compare-poesis">Attributable, ordered state-change events</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Verdicts</th>
              <td>Human interpretation</td>
              <td>Self-review</td>
              <td class="compare-poesis">Deterministic — anyone can recompute them</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Who it's for</p>
        <h2>Constituted for the people who answer for research.</h2>
        <p class="lead">Whether you run an agentic program, a lab, or the platform research runs on — the substrate carries the obligations you are held to.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-3" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
        {researchProfiles.map((profile) => (
          <article class="card card--feature card--static">
            <span class="tag">{profile.name}</span>
            <h3>{profile.hook}</h3>
            <p>{profile.body}</p>
            <p><a href={profile.cta.href} data-profile-cta={profile.id}>{profile.cta.label} →</a></p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Where it stands</p>
        <h2>Implemented and designed, kept distinct.</h2>
        <p class="lead">The <a href="/solutions/sie">SIE</a> Definition Manager and Operator exist and run today; the Definition Blackboard, observation planes, and observability floor are in development. The argument is architectural — and it is the one our own agentic delivery process is constituted against, on the same stack. We partner with research groups to apply it: <a href="/contact">talk to us</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-cta" style="margin-top:1.5rem;justify-content:center">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/insights/poesis-stack-as-research-system"><Icon name="book-open" /> The Poesis stack as a research system</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/insights/governance-owns-the-concerns"><Icon name="book-open" /> Governance owns the concerns</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://docs.poesis.cloud/gsm/"><Icon name="docs" /> The GSM documentation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
